# Copy to `.env.demo` and fill in. That file is gitignored and never leaves
# your machine except inside the deploy tarball.
#
#   cp deploy/.env.demo.example deploy/.env.demo
#
# This is the DEMO environment — the one shown to clients at
# https://buszo-api.thinkcove.com. It runs beside the dev API on the same box,
# with its own PM2 process, its own folder, and its own database. Keep the
# database separate: a demo must never show, or damage, dev data.

# MongoDB Atlas connection string (Atlas → Connect → Drivers).
# The VPS IP 89.116.134.28 must be allowlisted under Atlas → Network Access,
# or the app will fail to start. URL-encode any special characters in the
# password (@ → %40, # → %23, / → %2F).
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://<user>:<password>@<cluster>.mongodb.net/bus_demo?retryWrites=true&w=majority

# Must match the demo API_PORT in deploy.sh. Only Traefik talks to this port;
# the outside world uses https://buszo-api.thinkcove.com.
PORT=3050

# Generate a real one — this token signs every session:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('hex'))"
JWT_SECRET=

# deploy.sh rewrites this to the absolute remote path automatically.
FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PATH=./firebase-service-account.json

# --- Image storage ---
# Driver photos, complaint screenshots and the banner. Same switch as kareez's
# src/fileStorage:
#
#   STORAGE_DRIVER unset (or anything but s3)  files on this machine's disk
#     IMAGE_SERVER_PATH  absolute folder the files are written to
#     IMAGE_SERVER_URL   public base URL for them — this API serves the folder
#                        at /images. Must be reachable from the phone, so on a
#                        laptop use its LAN address, not localhost. On the
#                        demo server deploy.sh fills in the domain.
#
#   STORAGE_DRIVER=s3  files in an S3 bucket instead; IMAGE_SERVER_* unused
#     AWS_REGION, AWS_S3_BUCKET, AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID, AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY
#
# Photos written before storage existed are base64 in MongoDB and still show.
#
# On the VPS, leave IMAGE_SERVER_PATH and IMAGE_SERVER_URL out: deploy.sh fills
# them in with /var/lib/bus-api-demo/images and
# https://buszo-api.thinkcove.com/images. The folder sits OUTSIDE the app
# directory, which every deploy empties.

# STORAGE_DRIVER=s3
# AWS_REGION=ap-south-1
# AWS_S3_BUCKET=
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
